      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Sorry, what is elevating permissions here accomplishing? To me this seems like a simple UI oversight. It is simply unresponsive while the Unity Editor is downloading. It also gives very little feedback that the download is progressing.\n\nTo me it seems like the solutions for these are to accommodate user interaction with the rest of VCC while it lets Unity Hub handle downloading the requested editor versions, and providing more of the metadata to the user. There is apparently enough to display the progress bar in the first place.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
